  "description": "Turning round and repeating timetables on the track network: nodes a (512, 1536) to g (6656, 1536), a tile apart, joined by straight edges e1 a-b to e6 f-g, each 1024 long, with dead ends at a and g, where a path never turns straight back. Alpha (1536, 512), Beta (3584, 512) and Gamma (5632, 512) each have a platform on the half tile of track either side of their node, b, d and f: on the edge before the node it ends there, on the edge after it starts there, so a 1-car train stops at the node going either way. A stop with reverse true turns the train round as the service leaves it, before the path to the next call is looked up; a train that turns at a station stands at the near end of the platform for its new way. A repeating timetable runs its stops cycle after cycle, cycle k shifted k periods later; after its last stop the next call is stop 0 of the next cycle. A period must be at least 1 and no shorter than the span from the first arrival to the last departure, and needs a stop; it is checked with the times, before the stations. Shuttle (rate 1024) runs Alpha 0-0 turning, Gamma 4-6 turning, Alpha 10-12, every 12 minutes, each run on its curve in the time its timetable gives it, from the scheduled departure to the scheduled arrival (Stage W2c), shifted by a late departure. A service dwells at least 42 s at either end of its timetable and wherever it turns round, starting counts as arriving, and so does reaching a call at once (Stage W2b): placed at Alpha arrived from the east (e2 backward, at b) and started at 0, Shuttle turns east and leaves Alpha at 0:42, 42 s late, on the 4,096 units to Gamma (308 along e5 at 4, its path all entered and so stored as [] with cursor 0); at Gamma at 4:42, it leaves on time at 6 facing west (1020 along e5 backward at 7), at Alpha at 10; leaving Alpha at 12 it reaches stop 0 of cycle 1 at once (it stands at Alpha's stop going west), where it dwells again, turns and leaves at 12:42 (302 along e2 at 13); at minute 1000 = 83 x 12 + 4 cycle 83 is 42 s from Gamma, and at 1011 cycle 84, which left Alpha at 1008:42 on a 240 s run, is 306 past d on e4. While it runs, setTrainTimetable is refused. Late is placed at Beta arrived from the west at minute 1000 and runs Beta 0-5 turning, Alpha 7-9 turning, every 20: a repeating service starts in the first cycle whose first departure is not before now, cycle 50 (Beta left at 1005); it reaches Alpha at 1007, leaves at 1009 turned east, and travels the 2,048 units to stop 0 of cycle 51 in the 11 minutes its timetable gives the run, 186 along e2 at 1010 and 372 at 1011, reaching Beta at 1020. Balance 1,000,000 less 6 edges of a tile at 1,000, 3 stations at 50,000 and 2 trains at 200,000. (Before F3 this ran on seven grid track tiles, where a train that turns at a platform tile is still at it, so Shuttle turned when leaving Alpha at 12 instead: 443,000.)",
